.setup-meta

# Anvil runtime sidecar — operator state appended on every run. Recorded
# dogfood deviation from the ADR-073 tracked-anvil/ posture (constant
# self-dogfooding churn); `anvil doctor`'s state-boundary check will warn
# here by design — the warn is honest, the justification lives in ADR-073.
anvil/kindling/
anvil/witness/
# Exception-store write lock (EXCEPT-007) — runtime artefact inside the
# otherwise-tracked anvil/exceptions/ governance dir
anvil/exceptions/.lock

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak

# Local review artefacts
review/
# `plans/reviews/` is tracked durable review evidence — council verdicts,
# triage notes, CI notes, post-merge and release-council reviews, family maps,
# and architecture review inputs. Lint tooling already excludes the whole
# `plans/` tree via .markdownlintignore and .prettierignore, so nothing here is
# in scope for format/lint.
# GitHub Local Runners
.github/actions-runner

# DBCON operator scratch — snapshots and exported CSVs must never land in git
scripts/dbcon/snapshots/
scripts/dbcon/*.csv

# Local scratch — drafts, throwaway notes, intermediate artefacts
.scratch/

# Stray Rust build/run output binaries redirected to the repo root (e.g.
# `rustc … -o rust_out`, `cargo run > rust_out`). These are debris, never source.
/rust_out

# APSCAN-007: canonical `anvil-plan-spec` CLI generates context packages
# under `.aps/context/<ID>.md` when `aps start <work-item>` runs. Treat as
# safe-to-regenerate cache output; the durable issues/questions surface is
# `plans/issues.md`.
.aps/
